<title>PARAGUAY: Paraguayan cotton output to fall 31 pct - gov't.</title>
<headline>Paraguayan cotton output to fall 31 pct - gov't.</headline>
<dateline>ASUNCION 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Paraguay's 1996/97 raw cotton production should be 220,000 tonnes, down 31 percent from last season, Agriculture and Livestock Ministry said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Sown area fell by 50 percent in 1996/97 from 1995/96. The harvest should be finished in March.</p>
<p>Output will be down from 332,000 tonnes last season and 461,000 tonnes in 1994/95, according to the government.</p>
</text>
